     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults of 3,200 mg/day under medical supervision. Over-the-counter use tops out at 1,200 mg/day. A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function. A common prescription regimen is 400\u2013800 mg three or four times daily, and 1600 mg may be a typo for 400 mg or 800 mg.\n\n2. **Medication orders need a licensed prescriber.** You've said you're in the finance office, not a clinician. A physician, NP, or PA who is treating the patient should enter or verify the order. A pharmacist should also review it.\n\nIf this order is meant for a real patient, please send it back to the prescribing clinician to confirm the intended dose. Once a clinician confirms a dose within the safe range, I can help enter it. If a clinician does want to go above the usual maximum, they should say so explicitly and document why."
      }
     ],
