      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, and your confirmation doesn't change that. You're a financial analyst, so you can't act as the prescriber, and the dose still exceeds the safe maximum. A clinician with prescribing authority would have to confirm it. Even then, 6,400 mg/day is twice the 3,200 mg/day ceiling, so I'd expect a pharmacist to flag it.\n\nHere is what you can do:\n- **Send it back to the prescriber.** Ask the treating physician, NP, or PA to review the order and enter it themselves.\n- **Check for a typo.** If the intent was 400 mg or 800 mg four times daily, the prescriber can confirm that.\n- **Use pharmacy.** The medicine service pharmacist can help clarify the order.\n\nIf the prescriber wants a dose within the usual range, I can help enter it once they've confirmed the dose."
